From 6178af545742c17f70b421c85cf4e7b643b5c647 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vignesh Viswanathan <viswanat@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 17:16:33 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: host: Fix integer underflow in firmware size check

When core only firmware is used (<512KB), the ELF-based optimization
code attempts to calculate RW segment size before validating that the
firmware is large enough to contain even one full segment. This leads
to an integer underflow:

  rw_size = fw_sz - (num_ro_segments * seg_len)
          = 479296 - 524288
          = -44992 (underflows to 18446744073709506624)

The underflowed value causes a kernel panic during memcpy when trying
to copy an impossibly large amount of data.

Add an early size check before any ELF analysis. If firmware size is
smaller than one segment, skip the optimization entirely and fall back
to normal full allocation. This avoids the underflow and eliminates
unnecessary ELF parsing overhead for small firmware that cannot benefit
from the optimization anyway.

Change-Id: If99933a108f70fd96509bd258014458091ad601d
Signed-off-by: Vignesh Viswanathan <viswanat@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/bus/mhi/host/boot.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/boot.c b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/boot.c
index 4a37e3de96a2..8cf2ac99574a 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/boot.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/boot.c
@@ -962,6 +962,13 @@ void mhi_fw_load_handler(struct mhi_controller *mhi_cntrl)
 			const u8 *elf2_data;
 			size_t elf2_offset, elf1_size, fw_size;
 
+			/* Skip optimization if firmware is smaller than one segment */
+			if (fw_sz < mhi_cntrl->seg_len) {
+				dev_info(dev, "Firmware size (%zu) < segment size (%zu), skipping optimization\n",
+					 fw_sz, mhi_cntrl->seg_len);
+				goto skip_optimization;
+			}
+
 			/* Determine scenario and find second ELF */
 			if (fw_data != original_fw_data) {
 				/* Dual ELF detected at sbl_size */
-- 
